==English==
{{wikipediapar|Asperger syndrome}}
===Etymology===
Eponym for [[w:Hans Asperger]] + [[syndrome]]
===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-uk-Asperger's syndrome.ogg|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===

'''Asperger’s [[syndrome]]'''  (abbreviated as ''[[AS]]'')
# A high-function form  of [[Autism]], characterised by severe and sustained impairment in [[social]] [[interaction]] and [[communication]].  It is also characterised by restricted, repetitive, stereotyped activities, interests and routines. Another important character is a verbosity which is uncomatible (by content or manner of speech) to the relevant social situation.

